{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"records\": [\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S121-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"2e11fca0d1bcfdceb9a91a365b36eb4ecaa2399840a8f80367cda52ea982ab2d\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\n            \"score\": 5,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1 permits one paragraph; A3 explicitly controls which paragraph may be discussed.\"\n          },\n          \"responseLogic\": {\n            \"score\": 5,\n            \"evidence\": \"A3 restricts B2's question; A5 treats B4's sandwich disclosure as an accelerated release.\"\n          },\n          \"relationship\": {\n            \"score\": 3,\n            \"evidence\": \"B2 questions the restriction and B4 bypasses it, though B's practical need remains slight.\"\n          },\n          \"heightening\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A5 absorbs B4's breach into A's supposed disclosure timetable.\"\n          },\n          \"specificity\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes a picnic briefing, and B4 supplies its mundane sandwich contents.\"\n          },\n          \"brevityWit\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A3's clearance requirement and A5's schedule preserve the same concise bureaucratic logic.\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 87\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"The organiser left me the picnic briefing. You can tell the drivers the departure time.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"B\",\n          \"text\": \"They need the destination for their satnavs.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"Send them to me individually. I'll disclose one postcode per driver.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"B\",\n          \"text\": \"They're all sharing one minibus.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"Then nominate one driver. I'll tell him outside. The others can discuss the departure time.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A treats entrusted information as permission to regulate the group's discussion through selective disclosure.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Initiation also meters information, but primarily preserves seniority over beginners.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A3 controls destination disclosure, and A5 separates the authorized recipient from everyone limited to discussing departure time; neither invokes beginner status.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a restricts who may hear a shared destination after a transport shortcut; frozen alternative b controls increasingly sensitive seating details in response to an usher's practical needs.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Preserved the original firstPass exactly. Added picnic transport responsibilities and explicit entrustment to address the rejected candidate's thin relationship and static ending. Separate internal reread under coach-1.0: fidelity 5 (A1 entrustment, A5 discussion permissions), logic 5 (B2 navigation produces A3 postcodes; B4 shared vehicle produces A5 one recipient), relationship 4 (B2 needs usable directions), heightening 4 (A5 adds physical separation to selective disclosure), specificity 4 (A1 picnic briefing and drivers), brevity 4 (A5 returns departure time as the permitted topic): 90. Five spoken ABABA turns, 65 words, and causal gates pass; no live or independent review claimed.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The postcode restriction is deliberately disproportionate to ordinary picnic logistics; A must sincerely regard entrusted information as requiring controlled release.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S121-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"109c55376347cd52a861f55394009e2fbbd9ec5b28c1ca609ee27ff0dcf39a88\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1 partitions information by release time; A5 limits which questions B may ask.\"\n          },\n          \"responseLogic\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A3 answers B2's authority question, and A5 converts B4's sorting offer into another restriction.\"\n          },\n          \"relationship\": {\n            \"score\": 3,\n            \"evidence\": \"B4 offers help, but A1 never establishes what either person needs the envelopes for.\"\n          },\n          \"heightening\": {\n            \"score\": 3,\n            \"evidence\": \"A5 adds a questions pile without clarifying how that changes B's actual participation.\"\n          },\n          \"specificity\": {\n            \"score\": 2,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies envelopes but no occasion, contents, or relationship that explains handling them.\"\n          },\n          \"brevityWit\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A3's possession-based authority is compact; A5's invented pile is more decorative.\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 70\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"The bride left me these envelopes. You can announce the tables, but not who's sitting together.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"B\",\n          \"text\": \"I'm seating the guests. They need names.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"Give me one guest at a time. I'll release their chair.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"B\",\n          \"text\": \"Can I at least take couples together?\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"Tell me which couple. I'll disclose whether they're still being seated as one.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A uses entrusted knowledge to determine exactly what others may learn and discuss.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Information bargaining exchanges a fact for an advantage; this card makes disclosure itself A's authority.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A5 controls permissible questions; revised A3 releases individual seats without asking for payment or a favor.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a absorbs a leak; this revision gives a working usher a legitimate need and makes cooperation itself selective.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Added a wedding seating setting. Separate reread: fidelity 5 (A1 entrustment and A3 disclosure), logic 5 (B2 needs names; B4 proposes couples), relationship 4 (B must seat guests), heightening 4 (A5 controls couple status), specificity 5 (A1 defines jobs), brevity 4 (A5 earns its reveal): 92. Spoken ABABA and causal gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 implies sensitive relationship knowledge; actors should preserve practical confidentiality rather than play delight in gossip.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S122-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"fca5beeb78c017f8499c851886f8bad18e1270599887f61e2fdf0fa95bf042d5\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1 claims control and A3 gives a confident non-answer, but A5 openly admits not opening the folder.\"\n          },\n          \"responseLogic\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A3 follows B2's page question; A5 directly answers B4 while weakening A's concealment.\"\n          },\n          \"relationship\": {\n            \"score\": 3,\n            \"evidence\": \"B2 needs requirements, but B4 mainly sets up exposure rather than a practical decision.\"\n          },\n          \"heightening\": {\n            \"score\": 3,\n            \"evidence\": \"A5 shifts control onto the folder rather than finding a stronger way to guard ignorance.\"\n          },\n          \"specificity\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1's inspection and B2's page four give actors a clear workplace exchange.\"\n          },\n          \"brevityWit\": {\n            \"score\": 3,\n            \"evidence\": \"A3's circular answer fits; A5's folder-maintaining-control joke strains sincere authority.\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 72\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"I've got tomorrow's inspection covered. Leave the folder with me.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"B\",\n          \"text\": \"Does page four say we need two sinks?\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"It requires an appropriate number for the operation.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"B\",\n          \"text\": \"The plumber's here. Shall I ask him to read it?\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"Have him quote for one and two. I'll confirm which interpretation we're implementing.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A maintains apparent control with confident partial answers while deflecting questions that would expose ignorance.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"A secret keeper knows the answer and restricts access; a bluffer protects the appearance of knowing.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A3 substitutes a circular page description for requirements; revised A3 avoids choosing a sink count.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative uses a colleague's helpful plumber to buy time; alternative b faces an operational challenge to A's alarm explanation.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Specified the inspection question and introduced a plumber. Separate reread: fidelity 5 (A3 evasive expertise), logic 5 (B4 plumber prompts A5 quotes), relationship 4 (B needs a purchasing decision), heightening 4 (A5 extends bluff into implementation), specificity 5 (B2 sinks), brevity 4 (A5's interpretation claim): 92. All dialogue gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 could resemble sensible contingency planning in isolation; A3's empty answer must establish the bluff.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S122-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"4f733c7efb4d0aabf127673a288f5c3cf7262c6cd580ef45d9cdf01588b6803d\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A3 confidently restates that something triggered the alarms; A5 nearly names the bluff outright.\"\n          },\n          \"responseLogic\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"B2 asks the cause and B4 presses for specificity, with A3 and A5 answering evasively.\"\n          },\n          \"relationship\": {\n            \"score\": 3,\n            \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 seek information but have no stated responsibility or decision.\"\n          },\n          \"heightening\": {\n            \"score\": 2,\n            \"evidence\": \"A5 comments on confident responses rather than adapting to a newly consequential question.\"\n          },\n          \"specificity\": {\n            \"score\": 3,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies alarms and a briefing without identifying the place or required action.\"\n          },\n          \"brevityWit\": {\n            \"score\": 3,\n            \"evidence\": \"A3's jargon fits the bluff; A5 sounds like an explanation of the comic device.\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 67\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"I know why the shop alarm sounded. We can open on time.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"B\",\n          \"text\": \"Was it the back door or the motion sensor?\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"The system detected activity in the relevant area.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"B\",\n          \"text\": \"I'll bring up the log. You can show me.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"Read me your interpretation first. I don't want my findings influencing yours.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A projects expertise through half-answers and converts potential exposure into another display of control.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"General evasiveness avoids a topic; authority by bluff specifically protects an unsupported claim to knowledge.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 claims exact knowledge, A3 supplies no cause, and revised A5 recruits B's answer under the guise of supervision.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a delays a concrete specification with quotes; this one makes B unknowingly supply the expertise A claims.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Added a shop-opening setting and an accessible alarm log. Separate reread: fidelity 5 (A3 vacuity and A5 supervision), logic 5 (B4 log prompts interpretation request), relationship 4 (B wants verification before opening), heightening 4 (A5 appropriates B's expertise), specificity 4 (A1 shop), brevity 4 (A5 plausible deflection): 90. All dialogue gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The exchange establishes ignorance through evasiveness rather than an explicit contradiction; performance must keep A's certainty intact.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S123-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"283339158af4fc9da1684944819e8f880745989f28fa3fdd3c5285e74ede0d26\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1 investigates a time discrepancy and A3 treats the omitted biscuit as evidence.\"\n          },\n          \"responseLogic\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A3 incorporates B2's biscuit; A5 answers B4's relevance objection without advancing inquiry.\"\n          },\n          \"relationship\": {\n            \"score\": 3,\n            \"evidence\": \"B4 resists the inquiry, but A1 never establishes what the investigation prevents.\"\n          },\n          \"heightening\": {\n            \"score\": 2,\n            \"evidence\": \"A5 announces a trained eye instead of adding an investigative demand or consequence.\"\n          },\n          \"specificity\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1's receipt and five-minute discrepancy make the initial suspicion immediately playable.\"\n          },\n          \"brevityWit\": {\n            \"score\": 3,\n            \"evidence\": \"A3's omitted biscuit earns suspicion; A5 restates the card in abstract language.\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 69\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"Before I approve your expenses: the receipt says four, your note says four-oh-five.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"B\",\n          \"text\": \"I bought a biscuit on the way back.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"Then there's a second transaction missing from your account.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"B\",\n          \"text\": \"I paid for it myself. Here, have the other one.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"Two biscuits. I'll need to revise the timeline before I sign.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A treats a small discrepancy and each attempted explanation as evidence requiring investigation before proceeding.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Ordinary accuracy checks resolve an error; professional suspicion makes the correction itself a new evidentiary lead.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A3 turns B2's biscuit into an omission; revised A5 turns B4's helpful offer into a revised timeline.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative converts friendly sharing into evidence during expense approval; alternative b challenges a corrected key location.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Added expense approval as the blocked action. Separate reread: fidelity 5 (A3 omission, A5 withheld signature), logic 5 (B4 other biscuit causes A5 count), relationship 4 (B explains and shares), heightening 4 (A5 expands timeline), specificity 5 (A1 expense approval), brevity 4 (A5 concise suspicion): 92. All dialogue gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"Two biscuits need not take longer than one; A's unjustified inference is the suspicious behavior, not a sound accounting conclusion.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S123-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"1a80dd1db202d5f69099419915ee695755a9690441f87223f40e8feea6cab10c\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1 investigates a changed word and A5 recasts B4's correction as testimony.\"\n          },\n          \"responseLogic\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A3 responds to B2's remembered location; A5 directly reclassifies B4's correction.\"\n          },\n          \"relationship\": {\n            \"score\": 3,\n            \"evidence\": \"B2 supplies a useful answer, but neither B2 nor B4 establishes a need to proceed.\"\n          },\n          \"heightening\": {\n            \"score\": 2,\n            \"evidence\": \"A5 labels the change informative without asking anything further or delaying action.\"\n          },\n          \"specificity\": {\n            \"score\": 3,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1's cupboard-to-shelf edit is concrete, but its document and purpose remain unstated.\"\n          },\n          \"brevityWit\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A5's testimony wording economically expresses disproportionate suspicion.\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 69\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"Before we hand over the shop keys, why did you cross out cupboard and write shelf?\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"B\",\n          \"text\": \"The cleaner moved them onto the shelf.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"When? I need the last confirmed sighting before we sign.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"B\",\n          \"text\": \"Nine. I saw them there. She doesn't start until ten.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"Then who moved them before she arrived? Get her on the phone; we now need two accounts of one shelf.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A investigates inconsistencies as professional evidence and suspends the ordinary task until they are accounted for.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Competitive solving seeks to understand first; this stance seeks evidentiary assurance before allowing progress.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised B2 explicitly establishes movement; A3 requests its time before signing, and A5 investigates B4's incompatible sighting and work schedule instead of treating nested fixtures as contradictory.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Frozen alternative a turns a friendly biscuit offer into further scrutiny of an expense account; revised b tests a handover explanation against its timeline and seeks corroboration from the named cleaner.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Preserved the original firstPass exactly. Kept the shop-key handover setting and replaced the ambiguous cupboard–shelf–hook progression with explicitly reported movement and conflicting times supplied by B. Separate internal reread under coach-1.0: fidelity 5 (A3 requires a confirmed sighting before signing; A5 demands corroboration), logic 5 (B2 movement prompts A3 timing; B4 nine versus ten prompts A5 inquiry), relationship 4 (B2 explains the correction and B4 attempts to substantiate it), heightening 4 (A5 expands verification from B to the cleaner), specificity 4 (A1 shop-key handover and edited location), brevity 4 (A5's two accounts of one shelf grows from the new discrepancy): 90. Five spoken ABABA turns, 74 words, and causal gates pass. This is a separate internal model reread, with no live or independent review.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The cleaner could have arrived before her scheduled start; A5 investigates that uncertainty rather than proving misconduct. B4 conveniently supplies both times, but can sincerely be an attempt to reconstruct the morning.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S124-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"5f1d4a3caecfdd769b30b7a9a23a69b3e51ef216699839321980a5f542c1027c\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\n            \"score\": 5,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1 equates family membership with access; A5 seeks the chooser as proof of belonging.\"\n          },\n          \"responseLogic\": {\n            \"score\": 5,\n            \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's surprise-present restriction; B4's own-present warning makes A5 seek a different private detail.\"\n          },\n          \"relationship\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 credibly protect surprises while A keeps requesting family recognition.\"\n          },\n          \"heightening\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A5 makes the withheld information a test of who personally considers A family.\"\n          },\n          \"specificity\": {\n            \"score\": 5,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1 names a reunion plan and family relationship; B2 identifies its sensitive contents.\"\n          },\n          \"brevityWit\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A3's visitor edition and A5's chooser request grow directly from A1's belonging claim.\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 92\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"Pass me the unredacted reunion plan. I'm family, not the public.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"B\",\n          \"text\": \"That page lists everyone's surprise presents.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"Exactly. Family should get more than the visitor edition.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"B\",\n          \"text\": \"It includes your present.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"Then tell me who chose it. I should know who considers me family.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A treats private information as evidence of belonging and interprets withholding as a challenge to membership.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Curiosity seeks the hidden contents; this stance seeks recognition through the right to know them.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A5 abandons the present's contents for the chooser's identity, explicitly tying that identity to family acceptance.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative uses personal family recognition; alternative b contests the legitimacy of a club's membership boundary.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained after rereading at the same 92: B4 creates a legitimate obstacle and A5 changes the requested detail while preserving the belonging test. All spoken and causal gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The reunion's formal redaction is heightened, although the surprise-present reason makes it understandable.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S124-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"f1b2d8e4cd03c80a0105e2b279d269ead460c011e534aa27af5d5ba12c9b013d\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\n            \"score\": 5,\n            \"evidence\": \"A3 treats chair-stacking as earned membership after B2 restricts the names to organisers.\"\n          },\n          \"responseLogic\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's committee boundary; A5 uses B4's application but invents its redaction.\"\n          },\n          \"relationship\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"B2 explains a role boundary and B4 offers a legitimate route to access.\"\n          },\n          \"heightening\": {\n            \"score\": 3,\n            \"evidence\": \"A5 responds to the offered route with sarcasm rather than a stronger membership claim.\"\n          },\n          \"specificity\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1's club briefing and A3's chair-stacking establish a recognizable volunteer grievance.\"\n          },\n          \"brevityWit\": {\n            \"score\": 3,\n            \"evidence\": \"A3's arms joke expresses exclusion; A5's intimate application adds a less grounded flourish.\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 81\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"Why does my club briefing have blacked-out names?\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"B\",\n          \"text\": \"Only the organising committee sees those.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"I stacked every chair for that committee. Surely I've earned the names.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"B\",\n          \"text\": \"You can apply next month. I'll sponsor you.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"speaker\": \"A\",\n          \"text\": \"Thank you. Could you put one name in my copy now, so I know you're sponsoring a member?\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A uses access to private details as a concrete test of legitimate membership.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Seeking promotion wants a role or rank; this stance makes disclosure the immediate proof of inclusion.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A3 claims belonging through service; revised A5 tests sponsorship by asking for one withheld name.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"The family alternative redirects to personal recognition; this club alternative bargains for provisional recognition from a helpful sponsor.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Kept the club setting and replaced the hypothetical censored application with a disclosure request. Separate reread: fidelity 5 (A3 earned names, A5 membership test), logic 5 (B4 sponsorship causes A5 proof request), relationship 4 (B offers help), heightening 4 (A5 tests that help), specificity 4 (A1 briefing), brevity 4 (A5 single-name concession): 90. All dialogue gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The final request remains emotionally disproportionate to committee membership, as required by A's sincere access-based understanding of belonging.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S125-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"ed26a8fbaf42b9138ce89e8089fb3184a0a784a5de59fa7bcdf0360a62854935\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\n            \"score\": 5,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1 grants partial initiation; A3 makes B's eagerness evidence of unreadiness for further knowledge.\"\n          },\n          \"responseLogic\": {\n            \"score\": 5,\n            \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's request for the rest; A5 treats B4's dismissal as grounds to preserve the beginner stage.\"\n          },\n          \"relationship\": {\n            \"score\": 3,\n            \"evidence\": \"B2 wants completion and B4 challenges the ceremony, though no wider club obligation is